                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I love this game. \nSomehow, to this day I feel like we still haven't gotten another parkour game that tops it yet. Though admittedly, my judgement may be heavily clouded by nostalgia, considering I was obsessed with the game as a tween.\n\nFree Running (a title so stupidly generic, it is just about impossible to find anything about this game anywhere online) is essentially the Tony Hawk's Pro Skater of free running, though it's more grounded in reality.\nYou have a selection of small stages to each complete a variety of challenges in - races, time trials, trick challenges, a silly crash dummy mode - or just explore in free roam, where you can gather collectibles.\nAdditionally, you can play the game with your friends through a LAN too, which is a neat bonus.\n\nI was heartbroken when I couldn't get my old physical copy to run on modern hardware anymore, until one day, out of the blue this bad boy suddenly popped up in my Steam recommends. \nIt runs perfectly right out the gate on Win11, no further patches or editing of any config files required, which is pretty rare for older games being brought to Steam.",
